# 中频词汇 List05
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List05核心词汇

{{consent}}{/kənˈsent/}{同意；许可}{The patient gave informed consent before the surgery.}}
{{consequently}}{/ˈkɒnsɪkwəntli/}{因此；结果}{The company lost money; consequently, many workers were laid off.}}
{{conservation}}{/ˌkɒnsəˈveɪʃn/}{保护；保存}{Conservation efforts have helped save endangered species.}}
{{considerate}}{/kənˈsɪdərət/}{体贴的；考虑周到的}{She is always considerate of other people's feelings.}}
{{consistent}}{/kənˈsɪstənt/}{一致的；持续的}{Her performance has been consistently excellent.}}
{{conspiracy}}{/kənˈspɪrəsi/}{阴谋；密谋}{The conspiracy theory was debunked by experts.}}
{{constitute}}{/ˈkɒnstɪtjuːt/}{构成；组成}{Women constitute a majority of the workforce.}}
{{constitution}}{/ˌkɒnstɪˈtjuːʃn/}{宪法；体质}{The constitution guarantees freedom of speech.}}
{{constraint}}{/kənˈstreɪnt/}{约束；限制}{Budget constraints forced the company to cut costs.}}
{{consultant}}{/kənˈsʌltənt/}{顾问；咨询师}{The firm hired a management consultant.}}
{{contemplate}}{/ˈkɒntəmpleɪt/}{沉思；考虑}{She contemplated the meaning of the poem.}}
{{contend}}{/kənˈtend/}{竞争；主张}{Several candidates contended for the leadership position.}}
{{content}}{/ˈkɒntent/}{内容；满足的}{The content of the lecture was very informative.}}
{{contest}}{/ˈkɒntest/}{竞争；争论}{The election contest was extremely close.}}
{{contract}}{/ˈkɒntrækt/}{合同；收缩}{They signed a five-year contract with the company.}}
{{contradict}}{/ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt/}{反驳；矛盾}{The findings contradict previous research on the topic.}}
{{contribute}}{/kənˈtrɪbjuːt/}{贡献；投稿}{She contributed significantly to the success of the project.}}
{{controversial}}{/ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːʃl/}{有争议的}{The new policy has proven to be highly controversial.}}
{{controversy}}{/ˈkɒntrəvɜːsi/}{争论；争议}{The decision sparked a great deal of controversy.}}
{{convention}}{/kənˈvenʃn/}{惯例；大会}{By convention, the president opens the ceremony.}}
{{convert}}{/kənˈvɜːt/}{转换；转变}{The factory was converted into luxury apartments.}}
{{convince}}{/kənˈvɪns/}{说服；使确信}{She convinced the board to approve the proposal.}}
{{cooperate}}{/kəʊˈɒpəreɪt/}{合作；配合}{The two companies agreed to cooperate on the project.}}
{{coordinate}}{/kəʊˈɔːdɪneɪt/}{协调；配合}{The manager coordinated the efforts of all departments.}}
{{core}}{/kɔːr/}{核心；果心}{Innovation is at the core of the company's strategy.}}
{{corporate}}{/ˈkɔːpərət/}{公司的；法人的}{Corporate culture affects employee satisfaction.}}
{{correspond}}{/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd/}{通信；对应}{The data corresponds with the earlier findings.}}
{{corrupt}}{/kəˈrʌpt/}{腐败的；使腐败}{The corrupt official was sentenced to prison.}}
{{counsel}}{/ˈkaʊnsl/}{建议；律师}{She sought legal counsel before signing the contract.}}
{{counterpart}}{/ˈkaʊntəpɑːt/}{对应的人或物}{The CEO met with her Japanese counterpart.}}
